# Build output lives in a named Docker volume, not here — see `./x`. This entry
# is for anyone who runs cargo directly on a host that has it.
/target/

# A Runner's identity and its cache are per installation and never shared. The
# key in particular must not reach a repository: there is no rotation, so a
# leaked one is a Runner that has to be revoked and re-registered.
*.key
*.key.partial
/cache/
.sandbox-fixtures/

# Throwaway directories from diagnosing a container by hand.
/.probe/

# Job scratch for the development stack.
/.runner-work/

# Compose reads this for variable substitution beside the development stack,
# and it holds the Server admin token. Never committed.
/.env
/.env.*
#
# **Except the example, which is the point of having one.** The pattern above
# is deliberately broad — `.env.local` and `.env.production` are somebody's real
# values under a different name — and it swallowed the one file that must ship.
# `git add .env.example` said nothing and added nothing until 2026-08-31, which
# is half of why this repository had no such file for so long.
!/.env.example
